The panel serves no static assets of its own — the logo and favicon come from
the branding API as absolute URLs, so this directory is empty by design.

It is kept, and tracked, because the systemd unit copies it into the standalone
build on every start:

    cp -a public .next/standalone/public

Without the directory that command fails, ExecStartPre fails, and the service
does not come up. Deleting the five create-next-app SVGs that used to live here
took the directory with them and would have broken the deploy.
